  <data name="Page.HowToUse.1" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>1) Frame up and take the first picture.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Page.HowToUse.2anaglyph" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>2) Start anaglyph viewing the first picture with the preview that appears next to it.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Page.HowToUse.2cardboard" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>2) Start cardboard viewing the first picture with the preview that appears next to it.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Page.HowToUse.2cross" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>2) Start cross viewing the first picture with the preview that appears next to it.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Page.HowToUse.2parallel" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>2) Start parallel viewing the first picture with the preview that appears next to it.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Page.HowToUse.3" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>3) Keep your phone steady in front of you and slowly move sideways in the direction CrossCam tells you to. Don't move too far - an inch or less for each foot away your target is. Also, don't turn at all, just slide sideways, or maybe even just lean.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Page.HowToUse.4" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>4) Align the first picture with the preview of the second picture and take the second picture when you like what you see.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Page.HowToUse.5" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>5) CrossCam will automatically align your pictures after you capture them, but it's not perfect, if you don't like how they were aligned, you can turn the automatic alignment off on the settings page. CrossCam also has plenty of manual editing options you can get to by tapping the pencil icon.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Page.HowToUse.6" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>6) Tap the check mark when you're ready to save.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Page.HowToUse.Intro" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>If you want to see this again, tap the hamburger (three lines) icon on the top left of the camera screen and tap &amp;quot;Help&amp;quot;.</value>
